  "summary_en": "Rwanda's 2022 National AI Policy sets a roadmap to use AI for economic growth and positions Rwanda as Africa's AI hub. It has six priority areas: skills, infrastructure and compute, data strategy, public-sector adoption, private-sector adoption and practical ethical guidelines. It includes an implementation plan with responsible institutions. It has no robotics content.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Six priority areas: skills, compute infrastructure, data strategy, public sector AI, private sector AI, ethical guidelines",
   "Establish a Responsible AI Office (RAIO) and add AI ethics functions to ministries' digital offices",
   "Launch regulatory sandboxes for AI and update ethics guidelines every three years",
   "Build regulator capacity to align with global standards and ensure public trust",
   "Join international AI governance platforms such as OECD AI Policy Observatory and GPAI"
